Backport DASH's owner flag transport for recursive native Make.

Origin: https://github.com/securely1g/DASH/pull/4
CPP transport: https://github.com/securely1g/DASH/commit/53e524a348589e2b2e0585a8c148bd9b2f8bc686
Linker transport: https://github.com/securely1g/DASH/commit/2f71c2d7b940b746e2b7cf16597ff0eaff765539

PR #203 run 42474481735 failed in dash_build. A matching native reproduction
failed to start GCC. Replaying its captured flags exported 148278 bytes in
MAKEFLAGS, above Linux's 131072-byte limit. Keep all ordered compiler flags
in owner response files before entering recursive Make. Preserve the current
DASH source version, dependencies, original Makefile and runtime payload.

The four-file owner change is based on selected 5c930540 and includes its
compile/link regression. The consumer separately supplies the compatible
linker helper over infrastructure .26; no dependency-version bump is needed.

